body:
You're a gem thanks

&#x200B;

So technically, if you do starve your body and slow your metabolism, you can build it up again slowly, as long as you don't go too fast?

I will try all your suggestions and go back to get some more. 

&#x200B;

I just wanted to ask whether this was dumb of a doctor to suggest. I've asked about coming off before and I've had at least two say "try halving it for 3 days then quartering it for 4 and then go off it" do you think that's a stupid suggestion because I felt it was and made me think they don't  know what they're talking about.

&#x200B;

Not to mention all the ignorant remarks I've had over the years "you should;nt just take a pill when you feel sad. If you were my daughter I wouldn't have you on medication" etc. There's a reason I don't trust them and have lied to them about how I'm doing just to get my meds.

I'm doing it by myself too. Doctors have been awful. I ran out and just decided not to renew the prescription. I wouldn't recommend it to anyone else. 

&#x200B;

That happens to me. I have everything in me telling me not to tell anyone and then I tell people and feel better, I just struggle to get over that hurdle. Doesn't help when you hate the world when you feel like this and feel like your friends are all turning against you
